Spec: Admin authentication

Purpose:
  Session-based login for a single admin. Everyone else is a read-only viewer. Has no persisted entity of its own,
  so it follows ./architecture.sdd without a domain.py, ports.py or repository_sqlite.py.

Owns:
  ./services.py
  ./routes.py

References:
  ../architecture.sdd

Depends on:
  ../shared/shared.sdd

Exposes:
  An admin guard used by other feature packages' routes.py to reject write requests from non-admin sessions.

Must:
  A login form checks the submitted password against `ADMIN_PASSWORD` and on success stores admin status in the
  signed session.
  A logout action clears the admin session.
  The password comparison is constant-time.
  Login is impossible when `ADMIN_PASSWORD` is unset or empty.
  The shared page shell shows a login link to visitors and a logout link to the admin.

Must not:
  The password must not be logged, rendered or stored in the database.

Tasks:
  [ ] Implement login, logout and the admin guard in ./services.py and ./routes.py
  [ ] Show the login/logout link through ../shared/shared.sdd's page shell
